animal(V) & barks(V) => not likes(jane, V) @ "Jane does not like any animals that bark."
dog(V) => animal(V) @ "All dogs are animals that bark."
dog(V) => barks(V) @ "All dogs are animals that bark."
animal(V) & jumps(V) => likes(jane, V) @ "Jane likes all animals that jump."
animal(V) & has_legs(V) => jumps(V) @ "If an animal has legs, then it jumps."
animal(V) & terricolous(V) => has_legs(V) @ "If an animal is terricolous, then it has legs."
animal(kiki) @ "KiKi is an animal."
# cannot express: "If KiKi neither jumps nor has legs, then KiKi is terricolous or has legs."
? terricolous(kiki).
